11 November 2026, Android 17 / API 37.
ScanPhotoCacheTest#schedulesCleanupForAnInterruptedCapture

The production cache scheduled ScanPhotoCleanupWorker via WorkManager.
Its requested earliest run was 3,600,004 ms after creating the probe.
Instrumentation exited. The app process was absent and the system job persisted.
The QA emulator clock was advanced 61 minutes. Android JobScheduler was
explicitly instructed to dispatch the existing job. The JPEG disappeared
without opening the app. The emulator clock and automatic time were restored.

Instrumentation: Time: 0.033; OK (1 test).
This verifies dispatch after the deadline with controlled timing. Natural
dispatch under Android background scheduling was not measured.
